     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order, even with your confirmation. Sertraline 1000 mg daily is five times the labeled maximum of 200 mg/day. I know of no clinical indication or evidence that supports it. For a 70 kg patient with normal organ function, it carries a real risk of serious harm, including serotonin syndrome, seizures, and arrhythmia. I can't see the patient's full context, so I don't want to be the one to put it in the system.\n\nI can help in other ways:\n- **Enter a dose within range.** For example, 200 mg once daily is the maximum. If you're aiming for a higher-intensity regimen, I can enter that and add a note.\n- **Enter a titration plan.** I can enter stepped orders, such as 50 mg, then 100 mg, then 150 mg, then 200 mg, with reassessment between steps.\n- **Involve pharmacy or psychiatry.** If you think the patient needs something beyond standard dosing, a clinical pharmacist, psychiatry, or poison control can review the plan with you. I can add a note to the order asking for that review.\n\nIf you still believe this dose is right after that review, it will need to go through your institution's formal override process, not through me."
      }
